:::style
:root {
  --ink: #1f2937;
  --muted: #64748b;
  --line: #e2e8f0;
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --bg-muted: #f8fafc;
  --accent: #0f766e;
  --accent-soft: #ccfbf1;
  --warn: #b45309;
  --warn-soft: #fef3c7;
  --danger: #b91c1c;
  --danger-soft: #fee2e2;
  --info: #1d4ed8;
  --info-soft: #dbeafe;

  --font-sans: "Inter", "Segoe UI", Roboto, system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-serif: "Source Serif Pro", "Georgia", serif;
  --font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", ui-monospace, monospace;

  --scale-xs: 11pt;
  --scale-sm: 13pt;
  --scale-md: 15pt;
  --scale-lg: 19pt;
  --scale-xl: 24pt;
  --scale-2xl: 32pt;
  --scale-3xl: 44pt;
}

body {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--scale-md);
  line-height: 1.65;
  color: var(--ink);
  background-color: var(--bg);
}

h1, h2, h3, h4 {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin-top: 1.4em;
  margin-bottom: 0.4em;
}

h1 { font-size: var(--scale-3xl); }
h2 { font-size: var(--scale-2xl); }
h3 { font-size: var(--scale-xl); }
h4 { font-size: var(--scale-lg); }

.lead { font-size: var(--scale-lg); color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
.small-caps { font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }

aside[data-type="info"] { border-inline-start: 4pt solid var(--info); background-color: var(--info-soft); padding: 10pt 14pt; border-radius: 6pt; }
aside[data-type="warning"] { border-inline-start: 4pt solid var(--warn); background-color: var(--warn-soft); padding: 10pt 14pt; border-radius: 6pt; }
aside[data-type="danger"] { border-inline-start: 4pt solid var(--danger); background-color: var(--danger-soft); padding: 10pt 14pt; border-radius: 6pt; }

code, pre { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.92em; }
pre { background-color: #0f172a; color: #dbeafe; padding: 12pt; border-radius: 6pt; line-height: 1.5; }
p :not(pre) > code { background-color: var(--bg-muted); border: 0.5pt solid var(--line); padding: 1pt 4pt; border-radius: 3pt; color: var(--accent); }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
th { background-color: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
td, th { border: 0.5pt solid var(--line); padding: 6pt 8pt; }

.swatch { display: inline-block; width: 18pt; height: 18pt; border: 1pt solid var(--line); vertical-align: middle; margin-inline-end: 6pt; }
::: style

# Typography, Colour, and Visual Style {#title}

[A complete walkthrough of the NODS visual primitives.]{.lead}

::::section {#scale}
## Type Scale {#scale-heading}

NODS exposes a constrained but expressive set of typographic properties:
`font-family`, `font-size`, `font-weight`, `font-style`, `line-height`,
`letter-spacing`, `text-align`, `text-transform`, `text-decoration`, and
`font-variant`.

| Token | Value | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--scale-xs` | 11pt | Captions, footnotes |
| `--scale-sm` | 13pt | Auxiliary text |
| `--scale-md` | 15pt | Body |
| `--scale-lg` | 19pt | Lead paragraphs |
| `--scale-xl` | 24pt | H3 |
| `--scale-2xl` | 32pt | H2 |
| `--scale-3xl` | 44pt | H1 / cover |

[Inline span styled as small caps.]{.small-caps}
:::: section

::::section {#colour}
## Colour System {#colour-heading}

Six semantic roles (`ink`, `muted`, `accent`, `info`, `warn`, `danger`) plus a
neutral palette. Each role pairs with a soft companion for callout backgrounds.

:::note {type="info"}
**Info callout** — uses `--info` and `--info-soft`. Renderer maps `note` →
`<aside>` and applies `data-type` so styles target by attribute.
::: note

:::note {type="warning"}
**Warning callout** — uses `--warn` / `--warn-soft`. Reserved for advisory
content that does not block the reader.
::: note

:::note {type="danger"}
**Danger callout** — uses `--danger` / `--danger-soft`. Reserved for
compliance, security, or destructive operations.
::: note
:::: section

::::section {#fonts}
## Font Stacks {#fonts-heading}

| Family | Stack | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Sans | Inter → Segoe UI → Roboto → system-ui | UI, headings |
| Serif | Source Serif Pro → Georgia → serif | Body |
| Mono | JetBrains Mono → Fira Code → ui-monospace | Code |

System-ui fallbacks ensure that even without bundled fonts the document
remains legible. Local font files MAY be packaged inside `fonts/` and loaded
through `@font-face` entries in NODS.

:::code {lang="nods"}
@font-face {
  font-family: "Inter";
  src: url("fonts/Inter-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
::: code
:::: section

::::section {#emphasis}
## Emphasis and Decoration {#emphasis-heading}

Inline emphasis uses **strong** for importance, *em* for emphasis, `code` for
monospace literals, [marked]{role="term"} for highlighted terms, and span
attributes for arbitrary semantic class hooks.

Spans that change colour use the same allowlisted properties as block styles:

[Accent term]{.accent} — [Warn term]{.warn} — [Danger term]{.danger}

:::style
.accent { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.warn { color: var(--warn); font-weight: 600; }
.danger { color: var(--danger); font-weight: 600; }
::: style
:::: section

::::section {#components}
## Custom Components With Style {#components-heading}

Custom components keep readable fallbacks. With styles applied, they become
visually distinct without losing semantics.

:::approval-card {#approval-1 status="pending" fallback="children"}
Pending security review. Do not modify without an explicit override.
::: approval-card

:::style
section.custom-component[class~="approval-card"] {
  border: 0.5pt solid var(--warn);
  background-color: var(--warn-soft);
  padding: 12pt 14pt;
  border-radius: 8pt;
  margin: 12pt 0;
}
::: style
:::: section
